00:03.880 --> 00:06.760
Okay, so now what is exactly part of the whole analysis?

00:06.800 --> 00:11.640
Well, we use it in order to find out the proportion of a part relative to the whole.

00:11.680 --> 00:18.320
Well, here we can analyze how an individual category is contributing to the overall in order to understand

00:18.320 --> 00:22.400
what is the most impacting category to the overall business.

00:22.440 --> 00:23.600
So now for the formula.

00:23.600 --> 00:24.480
It is very simple.

00:24.480 --> 00:30.280
You have to go and pick one of your measures, divide it by the total of the measure, and then multiply

00:30.280 --> 00:34.240
it by 100 in order to find the percentage by specific dimension.

00:34.240 --> 00:35.880
Like for example, if you take the sales.

00:35.880 --> 00:41.040
So you divide the sales by the total sales multiplied by 100 by the category.

00:41.040 --> 00:46.680
Or if you take the quantity divided by the total quantity and then find the percentage by a country.

00:46.680 --> 00:49.960
So for example, again we have our measure splitted by categories.

00:49.960 --> 00:54.000
But now instead of having this number what we're going to do we're going to calculate the percentage.

00:54.000 --> 00:59.200
So for the first one we're going to take the 200 divided by 600 multiply it by 100.

00:59.200 --> 01:01.400
So we're going to get the percentage 33.

01:01.400 --> 01:06.740
So once we do that for the all categories it's going to be now very easy to see that the category B

01:06.780 --> 01:12.740
it is contributing to the overall number by 50%, which makes it, of course, a top performer.

01:12.740 --> 01:15.540
So you can visual it in your head as like a pie chart.

01:15.540 --> 01:19.540
And you can see how each part is contributing to the whole pie chart.

01:19.540 --> 01:24.420
And with that, it can help us to understand the importance of each category to our business.

01:24.420 --> 01:29.380
So now let's go and apply this formula to our measures in order to understand the importance of our

01:29.380 --> 01:30.100
categories.

01:30.100 --> 01:30.820
So let's go.

01:30.860 --> 01:31.020
Okay.

